# Fleet settings: one "name value" per line. Every line is optional; each line below shows what the
# fleet does when it is missing. Take the # off a line to change it. Read at each use: a change
# applies at once, with no restart.
#notify-wait on        # desktop notification when an agent asks you something
#notify-done on        # ... and when an agent finishes a turn that took a while
#notify-after 30       # how many seconds a turn must have taken for that
#limit-warn 90         # warn once the pane's account has used this share (percent) of a plan limit
#start-gap 2           # seconds between one agent's start and the next after a restart
#start-agent claude   # what a new project tab starts: claude, or ask = a list to pick from (Claude,
                      # Gemini, Codex, Antigravity, Copilot, OpenCode, a terminal); a tab the saved layout brings back keeps its agent
#log-md off           # chat log: off = one file per project (logs/acf/acf.db); on = also one readable .md file per thread
#rules enforce        # TokenOps projects (afc-rules): enforce = a broken hard rule sends the agent back, once a turn;
                      # report = only shown in the pane header and logs/acf/rules.log; off = no reminder, no check
#rules-recap on       # one line under each reply: the rule check's verdict and what the turn did (you see it, the model does not)
#mem-wall 90          # no new agent or project tab once the fleet's real memory reaches this share of
                      # its agents.slice limit (one more would only slow the running ones); 0 = no wall
#ram-wall 90          # ... nor once the whole machine's RAM is this full (R: in the bottom bar); 0 = no wall
#cpu-wall 90          # no agent added by hand (split, agents --add) once the machine's CPU is this busy
                      # (C: in the bottom bar); agents coming back after a restart are let through; 0 = no wall
#splash on            # the logo's animation (5 s) in the middle of the screen before the fleet window opens (afc-splash)
#view classic         # how agents draw their chat: classic = native CLIs + tmux scrollbar;
                      # compact = Claude focus view (fullscreen, steps folded);
                      # unified = provider-agnostic ACF CLI UI (afc-chat: task checklist + 1-line bash bar
                      # across Claude, Codex, Gemini and Antigravity, keeping tmux scrollback/scrollbar)
#claude-view classic  # legacy alias for view (used when view is unset)
